From eb6ce9cdbea8b7587e9462b924136eb50435d1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:47:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] ggml: GGML_OP_REL_BIAS, so a 128K Inkling 2 context
 fits 512-token ubatches

A prompt batch's relative-position bias was GET_ROWS(table, distance) ->
PERMUTE -> CONT -> ADD(mask) -> CAST(F16). CUDA/HIP fuse that chain into one
kernel at run time, but the graph allocator still reserves every link at full
size: 4 + 4 + 4 + 2 bytes per (key, query, head), 23.4 GB of compute buffer
for a 131072 context at -ub 512 and 11.7 GB at -ub 256. Neither fits the
R9700 beside the 21.3 GB model, so the 128K preset ran -ub 128.

The chain is now one op, ggml_rel_bias(table, rel, mask) -> F16 per-head
mask, with the same kernel on CUDA/HIP and a reference on the CPU. Only its
F16 result is n_kv x n_tokens x n_head. Inkling 2 uses it for prompt batches
with flash attention; the one-token path and non-flash attention are as
before. Other backends do not implement the op yet.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL, -c 131072: -ub 512 loads (29.5 GB on the
card), -ub 128 needs 26.5 GB instead of ~31, -ub 1024 still does not fit
(8.1 GB). llama-bench pp2048 at depth, -ub 128 -> -ub 512: 32K 531 -> 681
tok/s (+28%), 96K 398 -> 468 (+18%); -ub 128 unchanged; tg128 53.9.
KLD against the previous commit, wiki.test.raw -c 512, -ub 512 and -ub 1:
0, 100% same top token. New test-backend-ops case REL_BIAS_OP (24 heads,
1025 distances, n_kv not a multiple of 256, two streams).
